      "text": "Given that $\\log_x 4=\\log_{27} 3$, we apply the change of base formula to rewrite the left side in terms of base 2 and the right side in terms of base 3:\n\\[\n\\log_x 4 = \\frac{\\log_2 4}{\\log_2 x} = \\frac{2}{\\log_2 x}, \\quad \\log_{27} 3 = \\frac{\\log_3 3}{\\log_3 27} = \\frac{1}{3}.\n\\]\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{\\log_2 x} = \\frac{1}{3}.\n\\]\nSolving for $\\log_2 x$, we multiply both sides by $\\log_2 x$ and then by 3:\n\\[\n2 \\log_2 x = 1 \\implies \\log_2 x = \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\]\nTaking the base-2 exponential of both sides gives us:\n\\[\nx = 2^{\\frac{1}{2}} = \\boxed{\\sqrt{2}}.\n\\]",
